Bitsy studies PyTorch's public API, documentation, and source code to reproduce
its semantics faithfully. Operator naming, broadcasting and type-promotion
rules, view behaviour, autograd conventions, and state-dict structure are
derived from PyTorch. Where Bitsy ports an algorithm or mirrors a structure
from PyTorch, that derivation is acknowledged here.

PyTorch is used only as a numeric oracle and performance baseline during
development and testing. The Bitsy Python package does not import or depend on
PyTorch at runtime.

